ar profiling of tumor specimens</article-title><source>Nat Med</source><year>1998</year><volume>4</volume><fpage>844</fpage><lpage>847</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9662379</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1038/nm0798-844</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Simon</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Sauter</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tissue microarrays for miniaturized high-throughput molecular profiling of tumors</article-title><source>Exp Hematol</source><year>2002</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>1365</fpage><lpage>1372</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12482497</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/S0301-472X(02)00965-7</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hoos</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Cordon-Cardo</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Tissue microarray profiling of cancer specimens and cell lines: opportunities and limitations</article-title><source>Lab Invest</source><year>2001</year><volume>81</volume><fpage>1331</fpage><lpage>1338</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11598146</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B12"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Imkamp</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>von Wasielewski</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Musholt</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Musholt</surname><given-names>PB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Rearrangement analysis in archival thyroid tissues: punching microdissection and artificial RET/PTC 1&#x02013;12 transcripts</article-title><source>J Surg Res</source><year>2007</year><volume>143</volume><fpage>350</fpage><lpage>363</lpage><pub-id p